# i18n and UI

- Every user-facing string goes through i18next. No hardcoded English in screens.
- **NativeWind v5** is required for UI styling (Tailwind CSS v4 + `react-native-css`). Follow `.agents/skills/expo-tailwind-setup/SKILL.md` when installing. Import `View`, `Text`, `Pressable`, `ScrollView`, and `Image` from `@/tw`, not `react-native`, so `className` works.
- Theme follows OS `Appearance` on first launch; user override in Settings. Palette hex lives only in `src/theme/colors.ts`. Metro generates `src/theme/palette.generated.css` for NativeWind `@theme` (`dark:` pairs). JS ColorValues (Material Icons, headers, SystemUI) use `useThemeColors()`. Use `ui` from `@/tw` for `className`. NativeWind v5 on iOS/Android does not resolve CSS `light-dark()`. After editing `colors.ts`, restart Metro. No raw hex and no `StyleSheet.create` in screens.
- Locale preference is `system` or a BCP-47 code from the registry. `system` follows the device via `expo-localization` (fallback `en`). Settings can pick System; the wizard still asks for an explicit language. Always resolve before i18n, fonts, or catalogue `resolveL10n`.
- Native app name (home screen label) lives in `src/i18n/native-metadata/{locale}.json` and `expo.locales` in app config — not i18next. After changing those files, run a new native prebuild/build.
- **Gurmukhi:** bundled `assets/fonts/NotoSansGurmukhi-*.ttf` via `expo-font` (not `@expo-google-fonts`). iOS UIFont needs PostScript names (`NotoSansGurmukhi-Regular`, …). NativeWind `font-semibold` is a weight, not a face — `src/tw` strips weight and pins the TTF or Apple Gurmukhi shows. Android still has the `NotoSansGurmukhi` alias.
- **Simple mode**: ≥48px hit targets, larger type, less chrome — including the JS tab bar. Off by default. First-run wizard: (1) language, (2) Simple mode, (3) notifications are required (playback + downloads), then the system permission prompt; (4) Android only — unrestricted battery (same copy as Settings, plus open later from Settings; Open app settings or Skip, then complete). Language first so later steps are localized. Same language and Simple mode values later in Settings. Tablet width ≥768 dp uses phone Simple scale; tablet Simple is one step larger (`src/hooks/use-chrome.ts`).
- **Keep screen on while playing** is a Settings toggle and also in overflow menus (except Settings). Stays active while playing or buffering. Re-apply on Android `AppState` `active` (activity recreate drops the window flag).
- **Unrestricted battery** (Android Settings only) opens system app settings so the user can set Battery to Unrestricted. OEM battery saving can freeze or kill a background stream **or downloads** even with `mediaPlayback` FGS.
- Android status and navigation bars: `SystemBars` from `react-native-edge-to-edge` in root layout. Do not add `expo-navigation-bar`.
- **Lock screen and headset buttons** is a Settings choice (default jump 10 seconds). Compact / Bluetooth / car follow that pair; the other pair stays in-app and on the expanded Android notification.
- **Offline banner:** root `OfflineChrome` on wizard/tabs. iOS `fullScreenModal` covers that — Now Playing / Settings / Bookmarks layouts mount `IosModalOfflineBanner`. Android still uses the root banner only.
- iOS `Pressable` from `@/tw` uses pressed opacity (Android already has ripple). Do not add a second pressed system.
- Use `@shopify/flash-list` for album track lists, Library, and any list that can grow to hundreds of rows.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Text>Library</Text>

// ✅ GOOD
<Text>{t("tabs.library")}</Text>
```
